const postContent = "<h2>What Most People Really Want to Know</h2>\n<p>When people ask about a salary slip, they usually mean something simple: <strong>mera haath mein kitna aayega?</strong> In other words, how much money is actually left after deductions.</p>\n<h2>The Five Things to Look At First</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Basic salary:</strong> the core part of your salary on which many deductions are based</li><li><strong>Allowances:</strong> house rent, medical, conveyance, or other support added on top</li><li><strong>Tax:</strong> the income-tax amount deducted for the month</li><li><strong>Employee deductions:</strong> confirm the applicable amounts with payroll; employer-only contributions must not automatically reduce employee pay</li><li><strong>Net salary:</strong> the amount you actually receive</li></ul>\n<h2>Why People Get Confused</h2>\n<p>Many employees look only at the gross salary and assume that is the real income. But the usable number is the <strong>net salary</strong>. That is why a clear salary slip matters for loans, visas, tax checks, and simply understanding whether the deduction amounts make sense.</p>\n<h2>What to Check If the Slip Looks Wrong</h2>\n<ul><li>Is the basic salary unrealistically low or high compared to the total package?</li><li>Are tax deductions in line with the current year’s slab?</li><li>Are EOBI and other deductions shown clearly instead of being hidden in one line?</li><li>Are allowances separated properly?</li></ul>\n<h2>Use a Generator If You Need a Clean Version</h2>\n<p>If your office gives informal salary messages or you need a structured document for records, visa, or loan use, the <a href=\"/tools/salary-slip\">Salary Slip Generator</a> creates a draft from your entered earnings and payroll-confirmed deductions. Tax and employee EOBI require explicit values, including zero if applicable; they are not calculated automatically. Other employee deductions can be totalled with a clear label. The tool blocks missing/invalid amounts and deductions above gross earnings. Employer review and authorization are required; a generated draft does not prove employment or payment.</p>\n<p>Inputs stay in page memory and are lost on reload. The print button opens a browser print dialog, where supported browsers offer Save as PDF. No employee templates, direct PDF file or image export are provided. See the <a href=\"/blog/decision-support/salary-slip-pakistan\">detailed payroll draft guide</a> for a synthetic example and dated source notes.</p>\n<p>Open Salary Slip Generator →</p>"

